<title>FRANCE: Rhone not interested in drugs merger.</title>
<headline>Rhone not interested in drugs merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone Poulenc managing director Igor Landau said on Thursday the company was not interested in any new alliance in the pharmaceutical industry.</p>
<p>Asked to comment on an announcement by Elf Aquitaine that it was desirable that the oil company's health and beauty products unit Sanofi enter a merger, Landau said Rhone wanted to focus on internal growth.</p>
<p>&quot;We are the seventh biggest drugs group in the world, we are the leader in the six therapeutic areas in which we are active, we have our hands full with the launch of new products and we are not at all interested in any alliance,&quot; Landau said.</p>
</text>
